{"id":"mega_explosion","compound_name":"Graphs::Aero::mega_explosion","source_path":"mega_explosion/mega_explosion.json","category":"Fire","author":"Autodesk","description":"An extensive graph which uses particles and multiple fuel sources to produce a big cascading blast with flaming projectile debris","documentation_file":"mega_explosion_docs_ENU.md","documentation":"## Mega Blast Graph\n\n### What it does\n\nThis graph uses aero with combustion and particles to produce a cascading mega explosion with projectile debris.\n\n### Inputs and outputs \n\nThere are multiple inputs for this graph: geometry for a particle emission which in turn becomes an aero source. Three other geometries are used for two more sources to create cascading explosions.  The output is the mega explosion aero volume.\n\n### Useful information\n\n- This graph is an example of a large magnitude blast with several fuel sources and flaming projectile debris from particles. Varying `ignition temperature` of the fuels is used to wproduce cascading explosions where the heat from one reaction is used to ignite others.  \n\n- Scene scale is important, as bigger volumes of fuel will explode more dramatically.  To achieve the goal of this graph, a larger scene scale is used.   \n\n- Performance is related to the `fluid detail size `on the source air node, and the magnitude of the blasts.  Fluffy solver `style` combined with vorticity required to produced the fine details of this type of simulation will also have a performance impact.","library_dependencies":{"Amino":"2.15.0.9","bif":"2.15.0.9","fields":"2.15.0.9","fluids":"2.15.0.9","geometries":"2.15.0.9","particles":"2.15.0.9","simulation":"2.15.0.9"},"graph_ports":[{"portName":"particles","portDirection":"output","portType":"Object"},{"portName":"preview_geometries","portDirection":"output","portType":"array<Object>"},{"portName":"ground_geometry","portDirection":"output","portType":"Object"},{"portName":"aero_volume","portDirection":"output","portT